2014 Mondelez Bid - Round 2 Offer Request

*         Asia to Asia & Middle East Africa

Hello WSI and ASI,

Firstly, thank you for all your help with Round 1 rates for the Mondelez bid.

Here is a brief summary on the IAS scope we bid on:

[cid:image003.png@01CEE433.8CC74E20]

*          More detailed port pair rates found in the attachment below.

Now it is time to review our 2nd round offer.

Mondelez has provided their targets for your reference in Column AA:  "Bid Price Target".   Their target includes OFT + BAF + CAF.

If possible, let's try to close the gap.  I have shown the Rate Gap Difference in the last Column BR.

Please try to adjust the rates where possible in Column AP, but keep in mind there will be another round and potentially a face to face meeting.


In addition, I will need your help with the following:


*        Double check the free-time days offered.

o   I did not receive your input in the first round.  Therefore, I had to input a "safe number" in order to be able to upload the bid.

o   In COLUMN BB to COLUMN BD, "Free Time Offer".  Please adjust this number matching closer to customer's target where possible and make note under "Carrier's Comments" Column BE .

*        Origin/ Destination Surcharges

o   We will need to itemize surcharges for port pairs that say the following in Column Z :  "This lane subject to detailed rate information. Please also download and complete the APAC Supplement."

o   I am waiting to receive the correct file format.  However, in the meantime please record the applicable surcharges and amounts separately.   We will need this information later.

*        Lane Capacity:

o   I did not receive your input in the first round.  Therefore, in COLUMN AT ("Lane Capacity (Max Containers / Week)") I inputted a "safe number" of the Mondelez volume we can support for a given lane.

o   If you want to support more volume please fine tune this number.

*        Transit Time:

o   I did not receive your input in the first round.  Thus, in COLUMN AS "Transit Time (Days)" I inputted an estimate based on our route guide on hanjin.com.

o   Please kindly adjust this number, if necessary.

DUE DATE:  No later than Friday, November 22nd , 5 PM

Please reply as early as possible within given due date.   NCM will need time to make sure all data is inputted correctly before the final upload.

Thank you in advance for your great support and assistance.

Regards,
Sheldon Shikhel
Corporate Account Management Team
Hanjin Shipping America, LLC.
Regional Headquarters
Tel: (201) 291-4678
Fax:  (201) 291-9832
[hjs logo]


